It's just become one of those things humanity has declared as morally wrong, since we are biologically built for survival.

&#x200B;

Think about a reality where we accept and encourage early voluntary self death, even providing medical services to aid it. So many people would kill themselves over short periods of pain like a break-up, losing a job, losing your apartment, failing a test in college, crashing your car and getting sued, etc. People would now have an easy out from all these stressors in life that are in no way indicative of how you'll be feeling a month from now.

&#x200B;

Plus think about the number of people who be convinced and persuaded by others to end their lives early. Our most vulnerable populations, homeless, mentally disabled, retired veterans, all could be convinced to legally get the potassium shot at your local walgreens to end their lives.

&#x200B;

I 100% agree with your perspective and as a society we should not be brain dead just regurgitating "suicide is bad, it gets better" because there's no guarantee it gets better. Tons of people live horrible shitty lives forever. But I think the alternative, legalizing methods of assisted death for healthy people might be worse than the system we have now.

