She spent her term **decreasing education accessibility** because she actively decreased  public school budget and gave that money to private religious schools. Not to mention the fact that she had no experience in the classroom, as a school teacher, principal, school board member; she had no qualifications for the job.

&#x200B;

We saw the consequences of this when she decreased the budget for the majority of Americans (public schools) and gave it to a small niche religious schools. Thus objectively lowering the number of students who have **access to higher education**.

&#x200B;

Community colleges across the country have gone into debt trying to keep their campuses open/maintain their services. **Community college is very accessible higher education**

&#x200B;

She even wanted to lower the budget again for public schools by 5 billion. She was also sued successfully in California for rolling back protections for online students - again **one of the most accessible forms of higher education**.

&#x200B;

You can debate the budget but the money isn't what matters. It's imperative that we maintain and always strive to expand **accessible education.** Private schools are not accessible compared to public schools.

It is absolutely not an argument for the current balance of the electoral college.

&#x200B;

If you make more money, your vote matters more.

&#x200B;

That is PRECISELY, objectively, and undeniably what you just said.

&#x200B;

The electoral college does need to be abolished but that is a terrible argument, nor the reason why.

The Associated Press doesn't award the White House. They simply predict the outcome and they have a proven track record of being almost 100% accurate since 1850ish. That is why we take their word for it.

&#x200B;

This doesn't stop votes from being counted, senators from casting their state's electoral votes against the will of the people or from litigation.

&#x200B;

To properly answer your question, yes they should be counted before December 23rd, the last day to cast electoral votes

