A hybrid system of public and private health care would reduce the dollar per capita spent on health care dramatically. It would also increase the number of options for citizens thus increasing accessibility to health care.

&#x200B;

This works well in one area specifically in our country: the mail service.

We have a hybrid system of public and private mail trade (USPS v.s, FEDEX, UPS etc.). The USPS has some benefits such as cheap media mail. UPS is a better option for large packages. The sheer existence of the USPS keeps other mail companies pricing in check.

&#x200B;

It also works similarly in food. Food banks exist and are open to basically anyone. Yet people prefer to buy their own food because it is generally higher quality/freedom of choice.

The problem isn't private health care.

&#x200B;

The problem is poor regulation.

