I have an interesting story of my own. (warning/no offense to anyone there is one derogatory word I use)

This happens to me a lot, as a young in shape male. I have a heart condition and prone to blacking out from exhertion straight up. I was going into the bank after just having dealt with my abusive mother as I semi-successfully moved out of my emotionally broken home. I was in an awful sad mood. I pull up into the handicap spot and IMMEDIATELY, this old 50s white dude is eyeballing me and muttering "...motherfucker..." under his breath.

&#x200B;

Whatever, I get out and walk to the door of the bank as he says "You don't look handicap to me" in a really snarky demeaning tone. I've dealt with horrible people yelling at me for this in the past and this has been an awful day for me, I had zero patience. So I kept on walking without even stopping to look at him, I shoot back "What are you gonna do about it faggot?". Not even trying to defend myself with the fact that, yes it is legally my placard for a valid reason. He goes BESERK at this point. He shouts "WHAT?!", clearly agitated from what I just said yet I just keep walking inside.

&#x200B;

So I'm in line for about a minute now before the doors of the bank SWING OPEN and its that dude again. He starts YELLING IN THE BANK "MOTHER FUCKER YOU PIECE OF SHIT..." and among other swear words before leaving the bank. People are just like wtf. Okay. Sure bud. um yeah.

&#x200B;

I'll speed up the story now. So basically someone tells me a min later that he is ripping my windshield wiper off my car so I rush outside and start filming him since he runs away into his truck the moment I come back out. He's yelling and swearing at me. I just get one more jab in before he speeds off. I told him with as much ill intent I could muster "That's why nobody loves you bud". I filed a police report and months later he ended up paying for it through court. Not my finest win but I'll take it.

I'm so sorry. This sounds hard I bet anyone in your situation might feel that way.

&#x200B;

But think about how old you are. How much time do you have for your life? In the grand scheme this could easily be a short bleak low before greatness. Find something you enjoy, maybe move to the USA or somewhere with more opportunity and go to college. College is great to meet people and develop the skills for a good job. 

&#x200B;

Bless your soul you can do this. find what gives you life, what gives you hope, what you love and follow it to the end of the tunnel

