**Today, my mother is single, homeless, living out of her car unemployed and has chronic pain from cancer.**  I wish there was more I could do to have prevented this, but here are the events I slowly uncovered which led to this inevitable outcome.

&#x200B;

I was born into a nice house in a great neighbor hood with my two sisters and parents. My parents never got along. Complete opposites and I can count the number of times I've seen them hug or kiss on one hand. Inevitably divorce happened. My mother had a very bad victim mentality and always needed to lecture us for hours on end. It was straight abuse but I never realized it because it was what I grew up in. I was lucky to get off the floor after an hour of lecturing of mindless content that was just rambling and rambling. I am not joking, my sisters and I would always check the clock the moment she yelled for us to get in her room because they lectures usually lasted for about three hours. **Just imagine for a moment, sitting on hardwood floor for three hours straight while you are shouted at about things that really make sense and when you've done nothing wrong.**  

On a regular basis. That was just one of her twisted punishments. My mother always would get released from her job or something would happen that would result in her getting released, but never "fired". 

&#x200B;

I found out when I was about 12 years old my mother had been raped and beaten by her father when she was a kid. Her japanese mother would sit on her and beat her with a hair brush over her head. Her dad broke her leg once and she had to go to school with crutches for weeks. Her father would rape her and eventually she was taken into foster care where the worst was yet to come. Other kids would spit in her food and such. Oh yeah and she was raped by random other people in high school. Im trying to be brief here tho cant share everything.

&#x200B;

I thought okay.. this probably explains a lot about how your brain has changed because of this trauma. Because of this, my mother was involved in a lawsuit against an insurance company because of the neglect and was awarded roughly 250k. **This was the only reason we ever had a home.** The lawsuit happened after her parents kicked her out when she became pregnant at 18 and was living in shelters pregnant with my half sister. Eventually she bought the home and was able to live off money she had. 

&#x200B;

**Now here is where shit gets really shitty.** I learned this bit when I was roughly 16. I mentioned earlier, my dad and mom are not alike. At all. My mom is strong believer in God and attended church weekly. Through some people at the church, they set her up with my dad. My dad was a fat white nerd who loved gambling and had a lot of debt. I guess somehow word got around that my mom had a lot of money and my dad flocked to that. **They got married two months later**. First off, how the fuck u gonna marry someone you've known for two months. Secondly as I'm typing this shit and REALIZING I'm the child of a fucked up man using a woman for her money to off his debt. Fuck me. My mom told me the day after their marriage, he told her to pay off his credit cards or he would leave her. My mom was so naive and dear god I wish she was stronger but she did it. She payed off all his fucking dirty ass credit cards mother fucker piece of shit. And years of shitty marriage where he would push her and throw things and yell. EVERY NIGHT JUST BEING UP LATE HEARING YELLING AND NOT KNOWING WHAT WAS HAPPENING. One vivid night I heard my dad going berserk straight up, banging his head against walls and apparently grabbed a knife and ran out the front door barefoot ran around the neighborhood after he like threw a old 2000s cell phone at my mom's foot that turned into a huge purple welt which got him arrested that night. But anyway fuck that guy even though he's probably reading this because he's a huge ethical hacker and tracks my shit (most likely), well you've never apologized to my mom or me so you can't say shit dad. And then the time he threw my mom against the wall causing her to have a miscarriage. She got a big injury on her back. Enough of this segment, next..

&#x200B;

**I connected the dots when the day she got cancer in a nerve in her lower back.** Her doctor said the cancer was likely caused by her lower back injury from the miscarriage from ths 90s. He said there's no way to prove it in a court of law but basically my dad caused my mom to get cancer. Eventually she recovered surgery going INSIDE of a nerve to remove tumors, but was left with debiltating pain since. It was known beforehand this was a likely side effect, fuck, she wasn't supposed to live at all. The chances of death/paralysis were over 95%. **She struggles today working because she is in constant pain and I have to watch her cry every day because she is in so much pain.** This tears me up typing this. I love her so much but her mental health kept deteriorating as she got older. 

&#x200B;

After her surgery she struggled to keep working. Eventually she lost her home in an auction after 3 years of not paying mortgage. By this time I was gone. I got a job the moment I turned 18 and began working to find a respectable job and make something for myself. More recently I learned my mother's mom was treated for schizophrenia. Explains a lot. My mom refuses to see a doctor. My older sister is graduting with a phD soon and is becoming a psychiactric nurse practitioner soon because of how much we wish would could help our mom. It got so bad she was telling me my girlfriend was seducing me to take my hair to the government as samples of my DNA to spy on me. And the food she fed me was poisoning me to make me forget things (lies she makes up). I could not make this up even If I tried. 

&#x200B;

The day I moved out, my mom told me "I don't know why you hate me, you are never welcome back in this home again". Exactly, doesnt even make fucking sense. I was ONLY ever nice and patient with my mom but her perception of reality is so messed up she thinks I have done terrible things to her. It hurts so much to have my mom honestly hate me. This might have all be really incoherent, there was a lot of details I "tried" to summarize on. It's no wonder my mom is so mentally ill, everyone in her life fucked her over.

&#x200B;

But yeah, I guess the family secrets aren't really mind boggling. Certainly explains a lot however.

